# Excluded from the repo-root build context (`deploy/Dockerfile`).
#
# `browser-image/` and `proxy-image/` are built with their own folder as context, so this file
# does not apply to them. `session-image/` is built from the root, but BuildKit reads
# `session-image/Dockerfile.dockerignore` instead of this one.
#
# node_modules matters most. Without it, the build stage's `COPY . .` overwrites the modules
# installed in the image with the building machine's: native binaries built for macOS arm64 in a
# linux image. `better-sqlite3` then breaks on the first `require`, with a message that says
# nothing of the cause.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# The UI is built inside the image. A stale local `dist` would win, since `COPY . .` comes after.
dist
**/dist
storybook-static
**/storybook-static

# Secrets and state: never in an image.
.env
**/.env
*.pem
*.key
*_deploy
*_deploy.pub
**/*.db
**/*.db-shm
**/*.db-wal
server/data

# Useless at runtime, and heavy.
.git
.github
.claude
.impeccable
.work
browser-image
session-image
proxy-image
*.log
.DS_Store
